{"capabilities":{"clause_scope":"unavailable","lean_elaboration":"unavailable","pair_scope":"unassessed"},"claim":{"alternatives":[{"matched_terms":["algebra","characters","complex","infinite","nonzero","separable","tensor","unital","without"],"method":"catalogue-text-overlap","review_state":"unreviewed","score":9,"statement_id":"r:The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026:cor:infinite-tensor"},{"matched_terms":["algebra","characters","complex","free","nonzero","separable","ultrafilter","unital"],"method":"catalogue-text-overlap","review_state":"unreviewed","score":8,"statement_id":"r:The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026:thm:main"},{"matched_terms":["algebra","characters","complex","nonzero","unital","without"],"method":"catalogue-text-overlap","review_state":"unreviewed","score":6,"statement_id":"r:The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026:thm:finite"}],"catalogue_claim":{"credit":{"kind":"attributed-catalogue-extraction","license":"Apache-2.0","name":"Will Cook, OpenAI Math Atlas; source manuscripts and Lean quotations credited to OpenAI.","pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","producer_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","producer_repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","sha256":"sha256:9fc9f6d23da85bb837e0d6f0e7907a46ef873d851a749e513c3ebdc6c756d905","source":"data/families.json"},"state":"producer-declared","text":"A nonzero unital separable complex <i>C</i><sup>∗</sup>-algebra is Jiang–Su stable exactly when its norm central-sequence algebra has no characters, for every free ultrafilter. This answers the Kirchberg–Rørdam character question. Also, the infinite minimal tensor power of every such algebra without characters is Jiang–Su stable, answering the Dadarlat–Toms question. ([Lean](lean/docs/299.md))"},"historical_statement_ids":[],"method":"catalogue-text-overlap","primary_candidate":"r:The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026:cor:infinite-tensor","reason"