ter-criterion-September-25-2026:thm:main"}],"paper_history":[{"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"papers/ebd89f560d95b84ca75b7697.json","pointer":"/manuscript"},"id":"p:The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026","name":"The Kirchberg–Rørdam character criterion","status":"current"}],"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","producer_scope":{"credit":{"kind":"attributed-catalogue-extraction","license":"Apache-2.0","name":"Will Cook, OpenAI Math Atlas; source manuscripts and Lean quotations credited to OpenAI.","pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","producer_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","producer_repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","sha256":"sha256:9fc9f6d23da85bb837e0d6f0e7907a46ef873d851a749e513c3ebdc6c756d905","source":"data/families.json"},"state":"producer-declared","value":{"rows":[{"label":"Kirchberg–Rørdam character criterion","statements":["CharacterCriterion"]}],"scope":"The Kirchberg–Rørdam criterion relates Jiang–Su absorption to characters of the central-sequence algebra. The formalized result proves that, for every nonzero unital separable complex $C^*$-algebra $A$ and every free ultrafilter on $\\mathbb N$, the norm central-sequence algebra has no nonzero character exactly when $A\\cong A\\otimes_{\\min}\\mathcal Z$. No nuclearity, simplicity, trace, or comparison hypothesis is imposed.","title":"The Kirchberg–Rørdam character criterion and infinite tensor-power Jiang–Su stability","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/299.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":"Clause 3 — the infinite minimal tensor power D^{⊗min ∞} of every nonzero unital separable characterless C*-algebra is Z-stable (Dadarlat–Toms question; manuscript corollary cor:infinite-tensor) — is claimed by the headline and by the scope note's title but is not stated by any challenge. Clauses 1–2 (the character criterion) are stated in full.","note":null,"reading":"reading:85f0e035a49e482fed79bc83","source_term":"NARROWER — UNDECLARED","state":"narrower"},{"definitions_to_check":"The Jiang-Su algebra is not Mathlib's: `JiangSu.Algebra := CStarInductiveLimit.Algebra StandardPrimeModel.presentation.system`, a hand-built inductive limit of prime dimension-drop algebras with explicit multiplicities (`copies p := (p-1)(p^4+p^2+1)`, `size n = 2^(7^n)`), so 'A ≅ A ⊗_min 𝒵' is only as faithful as this model of 𝒵; likewise `NormUltrapower.Algebra`, `MinTensor.Algebra` (spatial/min tensor norm via representation pairs) and the central subalgebra are hand-built (2.1k-line challenge file).","gap":null,"note":"Stated: `character_criterion (A) [CStarAlgebra A] [Nontrivial A] [SeparableSpace A] (ω) (hω : ω ≤ cofinite) : HasNoCharacters (NormUltrapower.CentralAlgebra A ω) ↔ Nonempty (A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] MinTensor.Algebra A JiangSu.Algebra)` (for unital separable A: the relative commutant A_ω ∩ A' has no nonzero *-character iff A ≅ A ⊗_min 𝒵; for unital A the annihilator quotient is trivial). Not stated: the summary's second claim, that the infinite minimal tensor power of every such algebra without characters is Jiang-Su stable (the Dadarlat-Toms question; docs only mention the criterion).","reading":"reading:7d3a488aae552974ee639d5a","source_term":"partial","state":"part"}],"readings":["reading:85f0e035a49e482fed79bc83","reading:7d3a488aae552974ee639d5a"],"state":"different-scope-descriptions"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners (.github/workflows/openai-math-kernel.yml), one j","name":"Carlos Toledo, cert-machine","pin":"9814e4c06281e34a113ce853d7d99ccce160b750","repository":"https://github.com/carlostoledo1891/cert-machine","source":"cert-machine","url":"https://carlostoledo.co/reports/openai-math.html"},"id":"reading:85f0e035a49e482fed79bc83","pair_review":false,"review_state":"outside-report","source":"cert-machine","source_term":"NARROWER — UNDECLARED","source_value":{"code":"NARROWER — UNDECLARED","confidence":"high","disagreement":null,"gap":"Clause 3 — the infinite minimal tensor power D^{⊗min ∞} of every nonzero unital separable characterless C*-algebra is Z-stable (Dadarlat–Toms question; manuscript corollary cor:infinite-tensor) — is claimed by the headline and by the scope note's title but is not stated by any challenge. Clauses 1–2 (the character criterion) are stated in full.","openai_note_on_gap":"silent — the scope note's title names the omitted result (docs/299.md:1: \"# The Kirchberg–Rørdam character criterion and infinite tensor-power Jiang–Su stability\") while its Scope section describes only the criterion (docs/299.md:9: \"The formalized result proves that, for every nonzero unital separable complex $C^*$-algebra $A$ and every free ultrafilter on $\\mathbb N$, the norm central-sequence algebra has no nonzero character exactly when $A\\cong A\\otimes_{\\min}\\mathcal Z$.\") and the link table lists one row (docs/299.md:15). No sentence says the tensor-power result is not formalized; the omission shows only by enumeration.","second_reading":"NARROWER — UNDECLARED","text":"The challenge statements state less than the headline, and OpenAI's Lean note does not say so.","url":"https://github.com/carlostoledo1891/cert-machine/blob/9814e4c06281e34a113ce853d7d99ccce160b750/certs/openai-math-statements.json","verdict":"narrower-undeclared"},"source_verdict":"narrower-undeclared","state":"narrower","target":"f:299","target_kind":"family-headline"},{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","authors":[{"name":"MathVet maintainers"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"Apache-2.0","method":"An independent, model-assisted, pre-referee reading of each family's challenge statements against its headline claim under a published rubric (PROTOCOL.md), with its own Comparator runs per challenge. Its protocol describes a planned error-rate study; this import does not establish that the study has been completed.","name":"MathVet","pin":"14c7f918cd336d0da03a02aae5a0eed4a429d4db","repository":"https://github.com/mathvet/mathvet","source":"mathvet","url":"https://math.vet"},"id":"reading:7d3a488aae552974ee639d5a","pair_review":false,"review_state":"outside-report","source":"mathvet","source_term":"partial","source_value":{"code":"partial","definitions_to_check":"The Jiang-Su algebra is not Mathlib's: `JiangSu.Algebra := CStarInductiveLimit.Algebra StandardPrimeModel.presentation.system`, a hand-built inductive limit of prime dimension-drop algebras with explicit multiplicities (`copies p := (p-1)(p^4+p^2+1)`, `size n = 2^(7^n)`), so 'A ≅ A ⊗_min 𝒵' is only as faithful as this model of 𝒵; likewise `NormUltrapower.Algebra`, `MinTensor.Algebra` (spatial/min tensor norm via representation pairs) and the central subalgebra are hand-built (2.1k-line challenge file).","note":"Stated: `character_criterion (A) [CStarAlgebra A] [Nontrivial A] [SeparableSpace A] (ω) (hω : ω ≤ cofinite) : HasNoCharacters (NormUltrapower.CentralAlgebra A ω) ↔ Nonempty (A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] MinTensor.Algebra A JiangSu.Algebra)` (for unital separable A: the relative commutant A_ω ∩ A' has no nonzero *-character iff A ≅ A ⊗_min 𝒵; for unital A the annihilator quotient is trivial). Not stated: the summary's second claim, that the infinite minimal tensor power of every such algebra without characters is Jiang-Su stable (the Dadarlat-Toms question; docs only mention the criterion).","text":"Only a special case is stated, or a co-equal headline claim has no challenge statement.","url":"https://github.com/mathvet/mathvet/blob/14c7f918cd336d0da03a02aae5a0eed4a429d4db/reviews/openai-math/fidelity-table.csv","verdict":"partial"},"source_verdict":"partial","state":"part","target":"f:299","target_kind":"family-headline"}],"release_id":"openai-math","remaining_checks":[{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:d47c76a368b15ed29c7cad4dd1fa4f878f567a7a53a288e99d321ee0ebea343f","grain":"challenge","id":"challenge:CharacterCriterion","title":"CharacterCriterion"},"kind":"scope-review","reason":"An AI scope draft has no named human review.","target":"l:CharacterCriterion"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:725ae5c53e55548a4a16be30c3437ee7a0e77355d79aa07c4229b057460a5d61","grain":"family","id":"family:299","title":"The Kirchberg–Rørdam character criterion and infinite tensor-power Jiang–Su stability"},"kind":"claim-identification","reason":"Lexical navigation candidate; catalogue headline identity requires review.","target":"f:299"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:725ae5c53e55548a4a16be30c3437ee7a0e77355d79aa07c4229b057460a5d61","grain":"family","id":"family:299","title":"The Kirchberg–Rørdam character criterion and infinite tensor-power Jiang–Su stability"},"credit":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","authors":[{"name":"MathVet maintainers"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"Apache-2.0","method":"An independent, model-assisted, pre-referee reading of each family's challenge statements against its headline claim under a published rubric (PROTOCOL.md), with its own Comparator runs per challenge. Its protocol describes a planned error-rate study; this import does not establish that the study has been completed.","name":"MathVet","pin":"14c7f918cd336d0da03a02aae5a0eed4a429d4db","repository":"https://github.com/mathvet/mathvet","source":"mathvet","url":"https://math.vet"},"kind":"reader-request","reading":"reading:7d3a488aae552974ee639d5a","reason":"The Jiang-Su algebra is not Mathlib's: `JiangSu.Algebra := CStarInductiveLimit.Algebra StandardPrimeModel.presentation.system`, a hand-built inductive limit of prime dimension-drop algebras with explicit multiplicities (`copies p := (p-1)(p^4+p^2+1)`, `size n = 2^(7^n)`), so 'A ≅ A ⊗_min 𝒵' is only as faithful as this model of 𝒵; likewise `NormUltrapower.Algebra`, `MinTensor.Algebra` (spatial/min tensor norm via representation pairs) and the central subalgebra are hand-built (2.1k-line challenge file).","target":"f:299"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:725ae5c53e55548a4a16be30c3437ee7a0e77355d79aa07c4229b057460a5d61","grain":"family","id":"family:299","title":"The Kirchberg–Rørdam character criterion and infinite tensor-power Jiang–Su stability"},"kind":"pairing-review","reason":"Recorded candidate or producer-declared correspondences have no pair-specific review.","target":"f:299"}],"schema":"statement-map-web/2","selection":{"headline_state":"candidate","headline_statement":"r:The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026:cor:infinite-tensor","lean":"l:CharacterCriterion","method":"Show catalogue candidate separately; use source-cited targets or unambiguous manifest bindings, abstain on unresolved associations, then use source-text navigation candidates. Prefer a producer main-result Lean object with an available target.